\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Period-preserving signed permutations}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let #{n\ge1} and let #{N_1,\ldots,N_n} be positive integers.
For each period #{N} occurring in this list, put
#{I_N=\{j:N_j=N\}}. A \newvocab{period-preserving signed permutation}
consists of a permutation #{\pi} of the axes with
#{N_{\pi(j)}=N_j} and signs #{s_j\in\{1,-1\}}. It sends the
positive direction labeled #{j} to direction #{\pi(j)} with sign
#{s_j}. Composition of these changes forms a group #{B_\Lambda}.
On the sites #{\Lambda=\prod_j\mathbb Z/N_j\mathbb Z} it acts by
#{(bx)_{\pi(j)}=s_j x_j}. Signs belong to the labeled directions
even when their two images are equal as sites. On each #{I_N} one
can independently permute all axes and choose a sign for each.
Thus #{B_\Lambda} is the product over #{N} of the groups
#{\{1,-1\}^{I_N}\rtimes\operatorname{Sym}(I_N)}, where permutations
act by permuting the sign coordinates.}

\p{Write #{r_j} for residues modulo #{N_j}. The associated
multiplicative character #{\alpha_r} of the translations sends the
unit step #{e_j} to #{\ue^{2\pi\ui r_j/N_j}}. The normalized Fourier
vector of \ref{fdip-000S} is #{\chi_r=|\Lambda|^{-1/2}\alpha_r}.
The action on characters is
##{(b\cdot\alpha_r)(x)=\alpha_r(b^{-1}x)=\alpha_{b\cdot r}(x),
\qquad (b\cdot r)_{\pi(j)}=s_jr_j.}
The \newvocab{orbit of a momentum
label} #{r} is the set #{B_\Lambda\cdot r} of its images. Its
\newvocab{stabilizer} is the subgroup
#{B_{\Lambda,r}=\{b\in B_\Lambda:b\cdot r=r\}}.}
